    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37816" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-ordĭno</span></b> , āre,
		1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to preordain</i> (eccl. Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Deus praeordinavit te, ut, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Act. 22, 14</span></i>
			.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praeordĭnā-tus</span></b> , a,
			um, Part., <i>ordered
			beforehand</i>, <i>preordained</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">causae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Acut. 1, 4, 44</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Act. 10, 41</span></i>.</div>
